{
  "case_id": "2021-21-439",
  "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner Michael Nance brought suit under \u00a7 1983 to enjoin Georgia from using lethal injection to carry out his execution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0000-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Nance alleges that applying that method to him would create a substantial risk of severe pain."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0000-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Both \u00a7 1983 and the federal habeas statute enable a prisoner to complain of \u201cunconstitutional treatment at the hands of state offcials.\u201d Heck v. Humphrey, 512 U. S. 477, 480."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Masha G. Hansford argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae supporting petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0000-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We hold that it is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A claim should go to habeas, the Court held, only if granting the prisoner relief \u201cwould necessarily prevent [the State] from carrying out its execution.\u201d Nelson, 541 U. S., at 647 (emphasis in original); see Hill, 547 U. S., at 583."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The substance of the claim, now more than ever, thus points toward \u00a7 1983. The prisoner is not challenging the death sentence itself; he is taking the validity of that sentence as a given."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That remains true, we hold today, even if the alternative route necessitates a change in state law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eleventh Circuit",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court of Appeals posited that \u201cit is not [a federal court's] place to entertain complaints under section 1983\u201d that would compel a State to change its capital punishment law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here, the District Court held Nance's suit untimely under that limitations period."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "An inmate must bring a method-of-execution challenge in a federal habeas application, rather than under 42 U. S. C. \u00a7 1983, if \u201ca grant of relief to the inmate would necessarily bar the execution.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court is looking too far down the road. In my view, the consequence of the relief that a prisoner seeks depends on state law as it currently exists."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here, by contrast, the warden and the commissioner are not free to use an alternative to lethal injection\u2014so if Nance succeeds, they cannot carry out his sentence."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
